#{[17592186475953 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475953 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132532" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475953 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475953 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${∬}_{D}2y{e}^{x}\\,dA,$ where $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475953 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9c36b7d-47cc-5c7c-bf98-1c203381319d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475953 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type II region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}\\}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y{e}^{x}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}2y{e}^{x}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}2y{e}^{x}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{e}^{x}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y[\\,{e}^{x}\\,]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y({e}^{{y}^{2}}-{e}^{0})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2y{e}^{{y}^{2}}-2y)\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2y{e}^{{y}^{2}}-2y)\\,dy & ={[{e}^{{y}^{2}}-{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =({e}^{1}-1)-({e}^{0}-0) \\\\  & =e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475963 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475963 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132388" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475963 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475963 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/9c/9c684a6eaf9961b441cb559656aa2689ed0f25f61add19094df16e617ece8daf.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $x=\\frac{1}{8}{y}^{3},\\,$ $x=3-y,$ and $y=0,$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475963 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c16e9cb6-870f-5672-9efc-e4072f4b672a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475963 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/2d/2dcc8a77fea8a9fd3e95022edcd86e0a040c54fd30d88a7931c0542fdeaefd0b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{8}{y}^{3}\\le x\\le 3-y\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}/8}^{3-y}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{3}/8}^{3-y}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
